# EKF-active parameter set: one of the EKF-active runs of the P00 probe (both runs use this set since the fork ruling).
#
# The pinned set (compat_base.parm, copied unchanged from the ArduPilot Webots_Python
# example at af852591) sets AHRS_EKF_TYPE 10, which selects the simulator's own state
# as the estimator. This file adds only what is needed to make EKF3 the estimator, so
# the estimator-health item has a configuration in which it means something. Parameter
# files layer in order, so every value this file does not name still comes from the
# pinned set.
AHRS_EKF_TYPE 3
EK3_ENABLE 1
EK2_ENABLE 0

# Webots R2025a exposes no compass device; the magnetometer EKF3 fuses here is
# synthesized inside SITL from the simulated magnetic field. accept-mission-12
# run-a ended with "GPS Glitch or Compass error" and "GPS and AHRS differ by
# 30.0m" before the crash detector disarmed it at AngErr=170 (roll inverted to
# pi) - the only estimator that has produced that failure class is the one
# fusing this synthesized compass. Remove it from the fusion and forbid
# mid-flight mag calibration so the remaining attitude source is the inertial
# unit plus GPS. One change-set: the synthesized magnetometer.
#
# EK3_SRC1_YAW 3 (GPS) is mandatory alongside MAG_CAL 5: pinned firmware
# rejects that combination otherwise - libraries/AP_NavEKF3/AP_NavEKF3.cpp:1180-1184
# returns "EK3_MAG_CAL and EK3_SRC1_YAW inconsistent" unless the yaw source is
# GPS. accept-mission-13 confirmed that rule the hard way (both runs refused
# to arm with exactly that message).
COMPASS_USE 0
EK3_MAG_CAL 5
EK3_SRC1_YAW 3
